<title>GERMANY: Kolbenschmidt 95/96 group net profit drops.</title>
<headline>Kolbenschmidt 95/96 group net profit drops.</headline>
<dateline>NECKARSULM, Germany 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   30.294  vs 45.684</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    60.704  vs 63.016</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share		 1.60    vs 1.70 marks</p>
<p>    Group sales				  1,324   vs 1,338</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    7,388   vs 7,106</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  36.075  vs 30.175</p>
<p>    Parent income from ord. activities   39.87   vs 35.422</p>
<p>    Dividend				     0	 vs 0 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German components group is Kolbenschmidt AG. The company said that the stronger fall in net profit compared with the slide in pre-tax profit was mainly due to an extraordinary tax burden of 14 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
